  "generated_text": "1. **Apply the Remainder Theorem:**\n   By the Remainder Theorem, when $p(x)$ is divided by $x - 3,$ the remainder is $p(3) = 11.$\n\n2. **Calculate $p(3)$:**\n   \\[\n   p(3) = A(3)^5 + B(3)^3 + C(3) + 4 = 11\n   \\]\n   Simplifying, we get:\n   \\[\n   243A + 27B + 3C + 4 = 11\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   243A + 27B + 3C = 7\n   \\]\n\n3. **Find the Remainder When Divided by $x + 3$:**\n   Using the Remainder Theorem again, the remainder when $p(x)$ is divided by $x + 3$ is $p(-3).$\n\n4. **Calculate $p(-3)$:**\n   \\[\n   p(-3) = A(-3)^5 + B(-3)^3 + C(-3) + 4\n   \\]\n   Simplifying, we get:\n",
